# Copy to keystore.properties (gitignored) on the machine that cuts releases.
#
# Generate the keystore it points at with:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore wled-climb-release.jks \
#     -alias wled-climb -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# The validity is deliberately long. A certificate that expires cannot sign
# updates any more, and there is no renewal path for an installed app - so it
# is set past the point where it could plausibly matter.
#
# Back the .jks file up somewhere durable before distributing anything signed
# with it. Lose it and every install already out there is stranded: updates
# can only be signed by the same key, so the only way forward would be a new
# applicationId and a clean install on every device.
#
# Keep it OUTSIDE the repo and point at it absolutely, as below. *.jks is
# gitignored so it would not be committed from the project folder either, but
# ignored files are exactly what `git clean -xfd` deletes - and that is not a
# command you want to be one keystroke away from an unrecoverable app.

storeFile=D:/keys/wled-climb-release.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=wled-climb
keyPassword=
